Z||000014||batboy||12-03-1999||10:36 PM||||Fiero56, you're getting us cave dwellers mixed up, it was me that said I had the braided plug wires.<P>They were in the high performance section of Parts America, which was formerly Western Auto, and is now Advanced Auto, so I don't know if they still carry them (I actually bought them several months ago).<P>They are Accel brand "Armor Shield Silicone Wire Set" part number 8010B. Supposedly originaly designed for the aviation industry. You have to ground the metal wire braids onto the engine block when you install the set. The coil wire is not braided. They sure look cool.||||reg||1
