Z||000036||batboy||12-12-1999||10:40 AM||||Well, I'd like to thank my sweet female friend who volunteered to pose for some pictures with my Batmobile. She endured a bitterly cold day to help me with this project, but she was enthusiastic and always had a smile on her face.<P>It was mostly a learning experience for us. Some of the elaborate shots we thought were going to be great were just so-so. She did a great job of trying lots of different poses and different outfits. BUT, we were cursed by a cloudy overcast day. Lots of the photos would of turned out much better if I would of used fill in flash or if we had a little sun. Even with an auto-focus digital camera, lots of pics were blurry, probably from both of us shivering.<P>Out of about 40 pics, we threw out all of the out-of-focus ones, the ones with cluttered backgrounds, the ones "that made her hips look too big", the ones where she had "a weird look on her face", etc, etc.<P>I posted the cream of the crop on a new "cheesecake" page at my Batmobile website (URL is in my profile). Just go to the main page, scroll down towards the bottom, and click on the Batgirl symbol. Just remember, I'm not a professional photographer and she's never been a model, so don't expect too much.<P>She has agreed to do another photo session next spring when we have better weather and when I get more work done on the Batmobile. Regardless of the less than perfect results, we both agreed it was a lot of fun (except for being cold) and we both thought it was a bit of a turn on. Hurry up springtime!<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 12-12-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000037||Monkeyman||12-12-1999||02:19 PM||||batboy--How cold was it?  I'll bet she was cold. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Why didn't you include your car in the photos?  Did I just miss it somehow?!?||||reg||12
Z||000038||Patrick||12-12-1999||03:08 PM||||<BR>Hey, the pictures look great. That's a helluva nice back yard you have!||||reg||10
Z||000039||fierosound||12-12-1999||04:29 PM||||Many photo album of cars at this site.  I've gone through a few, but haven't found any Fiero photos yet.  Lots of great photos of other exotic cars though!!<P> <A HREF="http://community.webshots.com/topics/100276_views_0.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://community.webshots.com/topics/100276_views_0.htm</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000040||Patrick||12-12-1999||05:39 PM||||<BR>Great site, fierosound.<P>There's an awful lot of images there, and they're not all cars either, if you catch my drift guys.<P>Sorry Kel, I didn't see a "hunk" section. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000041||batboy||12-13-1999||07:36 AM||||The temperatures were in the low 40's with a bit of a cold wind blowing when we were taking the photos. We also sort of attracted an crowd at times in the park where we were shooting the pics. One guy rolled down his window and told us we should of picked a nicer day. We agreed of course. Just wish some of the other pics would of turned out better. Like I said, it was a major learning experience and I hope to do better next time. I also found out that my camera was not set on the highest resolution setting like I thought it was, bummer.<P> <A HREF="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/cheesecake" TARGET=_blank>http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/cheesecake</A> ||||reg||1
