Z||000043||DaRkLoRD||12-13-1999||01:20 PM||||I'm not sure who's Fiero that is, I just found it on a web page sometime last year. The original image I have is smaller than that even, I had to enlarge it for the calender mockup. The only mod I've never seen before is the louvres over the decklid. Probably makes it look like there's a hatchback when it's closed. ||||reg||1
Z||000044||Scott2M4||01-04-2000||10:11 PM||||For those interested ... I have an update on the progress of the calendar.<P>First off, let me apologize for my lateness.  Things have been very hectic lately at work and home.  Mix in the holidays and an illness or two and SHAZAM!  Where did the time go?<P>Anyway, the development of the calendar is nearly complete.  The front cover needs to be designed (I don't plan to spend too much time on it) and four of the months still need one component each (see my next paragraph for an explanation).  My wife is running test prints at work tonight to verify picture quality and she is evaluating different methods of fastening the 14 sheets together.<P>The amount of pictures sent in ended up being too many to fit one photo per month but not enough to fit two photos per month.  I scrounged for a few "non-forum-member" photos but I still need four photos (preferably coupes as the calendar is currently weighted torwards fastbacks) to complete the calendar.  If you would like to submit a photo, please do so as soon as possible.  I hope to have this thing sent to the printer by this weekend.  If I don't receive enough photos from forum folks, I'll just scrounge more (but what fun is having a forum calendar with non-forum cars!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   ).<P>I'll be honest with you.  I literally threw this thing together in a matter of two days.  I feel the quality is pretty good but nothing worthy of sale on the market.  Please don't expect "show quality" this time around.  For 2001, I plan to start much earlier in the year.<P>Which brings me to the subject of cost.  I never intended to make a profit off of this thing and I still don't.  "Cost" plain and simple will cover printing and shipping only - I'm thinking about $5.  I hope that's acceptable to all interested members.<P>Please send me an email (privately) so I can get an idea of the number of members interested.<P>BTW, for those concerned that they may not receive the calendar before February, I have taken the precaution of NOT using member cars in the months of January and February.<P>I'll try to post an example of what I've got soon.<P>One final thing for those that have already sent me photos.  I didn't get some of your names associated with your car.  If you wouldn't mind, could you please send me a brief email (privately) that (a) contains your forum USERID and a description of your car and (b) states wether or not you wish to have your "real" full name printed with your USERID (if you do, please provide your full name).<P>Again, I apologize for any problems or inconveniences I have caused.  Next year will be better (that's right - I'm calling myself the official Forum Calendar Guy!!!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">   )!||||reg||1
Z||000045||Scott2M4||01-05-2000||08:18 AM||||Here's a low res scan of one of the months.  Don't worry - the real one has color (I scanned a black/white xerox copy - hence the lack of color).<P>I hope the format is acceptable to everyone ...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Calendar12.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000046||fierosound||01-05-2000||01:49 PM||||Get lots of Fiero pics from site listed in this forum.  You can also download an excellent calendar program from site in this thread as well.<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/000824.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/000824.html</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000047||Scott2M4||01-05-2000||04:12 PM||||The development work is complete.  However, I have two photos that I'm unable to match up with owners.  One is of a red 84-85 SE with black decals on the lower doors that say 'FIERO' and the other is of a red 88 GT with the license plate BNC2970.  Will the owners of these two cars please contact me?  TIA<P>More to follow ...<P>BTW, as far as that calendar program goes, I went to that website but it said I had to pay $$$ for it.  Did I pick the wrong link or something?||||reg||1
Z||000048||Cooter||01-05-2000||07:22 PM||||Wow! My car is Ms. December. Count me in for buying a couple of the calendars. Looks great!||||reg||1
Z||000049||fierosound||01-05-2000||09:43 PM||||Scott2M4<P>The calendar program is a fully functional (not disabled in any way) shareware program that works for 30 days after you install it.  You can always reinstall again after the 30 days (or buy it).  You can also do a search for security material for this program (or any other computer program) at <A HREF="http://www.astalavista.com" TARGET=_blank>www.astalavista.com</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000050||Scott2M4||01-06-2000||05:02 PM||||Latest update:<P>Initial test print last night looked very good.  I'm going to run one more color test print tonight of the entire calendar.  Unless corrections are needed, I hope to do the production run Friday night.<P>The following is a list of members that have requested (at least) one calendar:<P>fiero56<BR>superXmotorsports<BR>cooter (2)<BR>sdm1964<BR>sluppy123<BR>dano<BR>batboy<BR>DaRkLoRD<BR>turbo86se<BR>Monkeyman<BR>Wolfhound<BR>Steven<BR>ditz88gt (3)<BR>Bill Osmer<P>Is this list correct (a few of you have photos in the calendar but didn't say whether or not you wanted one) and are there others?<P>BTW, I won't spoil the calendar by disclosing all details of it but I did want to pass some data along.  The calendar contains 21 cars and 1 hot babe (thanks, batboy!): 11 coupes and 10 fastbacks (7 red, 4 white, 3 black, 3 silver, 2 yellow, 1 blue and 1 gold).  A pretty healthy mix ... if you ask me!  Hope you think so too.<p>[This message has been edited by Scott2M4 (edited 01-06-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000051||DaRkLoRD||01-06-2000||05:38 PM||||yep, it's correct at least concerning me.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Let me know when they're ready!||||reg||1
